  "hypothesis": "The original TFPT source chain (P1/S/Z/OS/Gamma) is a single, coherent reconstruction where the boundary kernel P1 acts as the primitive reflection-positive seed. The 'stronger integral selector' (primitive family charge on standard D/A overlattices) and the 'function-differential typing' (Riemann-Roch index gate) are not independent axioms but scoped consequences of this common origin. Specifically, the E8 completion is forced by the arithmetic of the primitive charge within the existing source structure, while the carrier rank (g_car=5) and family count (N_fam=3) are topological invariants of the same four-point seam divisor mu4 on P^1. The hypothesis posits that these two distinct mathematical results (lattice completion and geometric index) share the exact same source ID (the original pointwise local force family with variable bounded background) and do not require new global CAR clocks or free metric assumptions to hold within their respective scopes.",
